1
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,439
It's obvious this wasn't planned in advance.

2
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:44,439
Sending him away...

3
00:01:44,439 --> 00:01:45,680
What do you want to say to me?

4
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,480
If this is a good cop, bad cop routine,

5
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,560
and you don't mind wasting time,

6
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:53,159
I'll make a good audience.

7
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:57,400
To be honest,

8
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,280
a few days ago,

9
00:01:59,439 --> 00:02:00,879
I was actually a bit anxious.

10
00:02:01,359 --> 00:02:03,159
Though I tried my best not to show it.

11
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,000
But today is different.

12
00:02:05,719 --> 00:02:07,400
I'm not in a hurry at all now.

13
00:02:10,599 --> 00:02:11,520
Everyone who needs to be brought in

14
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,039
won't be able to escape.

15
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,759
Everything that needs doing will get done.

16
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:18,879
As for me, I'll just gather evidence step by step,

17
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,800
transfer the case to the court when ready,

18
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:23,199
follow procedure, and take my time.

19
00:02:26,039 --> 00:02:27,000
Loaded words.

20
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,560
You're trying to provoke me.

21
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,400
Do you know what it feels like

22
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,000
to sit at the interrogation table?

23
00:02:37,319 --> 00:02:38,800
I remember back then,

24
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:40,400
when interrogating Cao Liaoping,

25
00:02:41,039 --> 00:02:42,000
I was very impatient.

26
00:02:42,479 --> 00:02:43,360
Because I wanted to win.

27
00:02:44,199 --> 00:02:45,759
I wanted a clean, decisive victory.

28
00:02:47,479 --> 00:02:48,800
Now it's different.

29
00:02:49,039 --> 00:02:50,520
Although I still want to win,

30
00:02:51,039 --> 00:02:52,319
I'm not in such a rush.

31
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:55,360
Because I know what you're thinking,

32
00:02:55,719 --> 00:02:57,080
and I know how we can both win.

33
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,759
There are only winners and losers.

34
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:03,719
What kind of win-win?

35
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:04,759
Let's hear it.

36
00:03:06,319 --> 00:03:08,360
Some things simply can't be spoken aloud.

37
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:11,360
Just like when you're wronged,

38
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,199
you can't talk about it either.

39
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:16,360
Why didn't I come by these past two days

40
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:18,599
or conduct an interrogation?

41
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,680
Because I was acting as a screenwriter.

42
00:03:21,879 --> 00:03:23,159
I made up a story.

43
00:03:23,639 --> 00:03:25,479
If this story is true—

44
00:03:26,319 --> 00:03:27,599
and it definitely must be true—

45
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,039
because only then

46
00:03:30,719 --> 00:03:32,919
can the two of us sit here peacefully,

47
00:03:33,599 --> 00:03:35,400
saying things that require no extra words,

48
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,400
yet we completely understand each other.

49
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:43,439
Seeing how confident you are,

50
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
it must be a story with quite a twist.

51
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,840
When I first joined State Security,

52
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:55,319
everyone suspected me.

53
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,759
Only you believed in me.

54
00:03:58,479 --> 00:04:00,800
You even came to my place and told me something.

55
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,479
You said working in State Security

56
00:04:03,639 --> 00:04:04,800
means enduring grievances.

57
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,520
I didn't understand it back then.

58
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,120
I thought enduring grievances meant being misunderstood,

59
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:11,199
framed,

60
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,680
and taking abuse you don't deserve.

61
00:04:15,639 --> 00:04:16,319
That wasn't it.

62
00:04:17,399 --> 00:04:18,560
Those things are far too minor.

63
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,439
That's because you haven't suffered enough.

64
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,480
When even my wife doubted me,

65
00:04:24,959 --> 00:04:26,160
only you believed in me.

66
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:28,040
All these years,

67
00:04:29,439 --> 00:04:30,639
I've been suspecting you.

68
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,319
I'm sorry.

69
00:04:41,439 --> 00:04:42,439
Don't apologize.

70
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:45,160
A smart State Security officer

71
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,160
never says sorry

72
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:49,399
to an unrepentant prisoner.

73
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:54,879
All these years,

74
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:58,160
do you know how much I've hated you?

75
00:04:59,279 --> 00:05:00,160
I hate you

76
00:05:00,959 --> 00:05:03,160
for going to such lengths to guide me,

77
00:05:03,639 --> 00:05:04,959
only to defect halfway through.

78
00:05:06,879 --> 00:05:07,600
I hate you

79
00:05:08,639 --> 00:05:10,519
for being the mentor I respected most,

80
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,920
only to become the enemy I must investigate.

81
00:05:17,439 --> 00:05:18,439
Yet while hating me,

82
00:05:19,199 --> 00:05:21,079
you still remembered what I taught you.

83
00:05:21,439 --> 00:05:22,759
Grasping the details,

84
00:05:22,759 --> 00:05:23,879
insight into human nature,

85
00:05:23,879 --> 00:05:25,160
anticipating risks.

86
00:05:26,279 --> 00:05:27,560
You learned thoroughly and remembered well.

87
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,519
That's why you never stumbled.

88
00:05:31,639 --> 00:05:32,839
A lot of people hate you.

89
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:35,639
All your relatives,

90
00:05:36,399 --> 00:05:37,399
your family,

91
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:41,000
even the colleagues who donated blood for you.

92
00:05:41,879 --> 00:05:43,279
Everyone wants you dead.

93
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:46,000
No one cares how glorious you once were,

94
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,040
or how much merit you earned.

95
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,399
Once you stepped into this interrogation room,

96
00:05:51,879 --> 00:05:53,639
you were branded a traitor.

97
00:05:54,879 --> 00:05:55,759
From sentencing

98
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:57,560
to imprisonment,

99
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:00,560
until you're completely forgotten,

100
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,839
you will always be a traitor.

101
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,639
You understood all of this,

102
00:06:05,759 --> 00:06:07,439
yet you still pushed every step

103
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,720
to the absolute limit.

104
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,600
That's quite a story you made up,

105
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:23,000
but interrogations aren't judged on literary flair.

106
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,000
It comes down to evidence.

107
00:06:27,879 --> 00:06:29,079
Some evidence

108
00:06:31,279 --> 00:06:32,519
can never be brought to light.

109
00:06:37,079 --> 00:06:37,879
Brother Qi.

110
00:06:40,319 --> 00:06:41,160
Thanks for your hard work.

111
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,279
Ever since my first day on the job,

112
00:06:59,079 --> 00:07:00,920
I've wondered why we work so hard every day.

113
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,079
What is it all for?

114
00:07:03,079 --> 00:07:04,519
For that meager paycheck?

115
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:05,959
For reputation?

116
00:07:07,199 --> 00:07:09,279
For the vanity of wearing a police uniform?

117
00:07:11,439 --> 00:07:12,360
Once you figure that out,

118
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:14,600
it doesn't feel hard at all.

119
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,319
Years ago, there was a man

120
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,000
who went from the mainland overseas,

121
00:07:21,439 --> 00:07:22,800
and stayed there for decades.

122
00:07:24,199 --> 00:07:25,360
When he left,

123
00:07:26,079 --> 00:07:27,600
he was as young as you were when you first arrived.

124
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,600
Even as an old man, he couldn't return.

125
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,720
His health was failing, too.

126
00:07:34,199 --> 00:07:35,279
Someone asked him,

127
00:07:35,839 --> 00:07:37,519
"What if you die here,

128
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,480
and can only go back as ashes?

129
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:40,759
What will you do?"

130
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,360
He said it didn't matter,

131
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,839
because there was no other choice.

132
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,319
This is the work we do.

133
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,360
Even if you weep,

134
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:51,360
you must cover your mouth.

135
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:53,680
This is our destiny.

136
00:08:02,959 --> 00:08:04,000
I just want to work under you,

137
00:08:05,399 --> 00:08:06,360
until you retire.

138
00:08:10,959 --> 00:08:12,279
I've already retired.

139
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:15,079
Don't sell yourself short.

140
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,160
The Second Division will rely on you from now on.

141
00:08:18,959 --> 00:08:21,199
That intel you bought from me before—

142
00:08:21,519 --> 00:08:22,839
you have to connect the dots.

143
00:08:23,759 --> 00:08:25,360
Use your head to analyze it.

144
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:26,920
Don't just look at the points.

145
00:08:27,439 --> 00:08:28,079
Look at the lines.

146
00:08:28,639 --> 00:08:29,680
The intel itself isn't what matters.

147
00:08:29,959 --> 00:08:31,240
The way of thinking is what matters most.

148
00:08:31,959 --> 00:08:33,320
In five years, ten years...

149
00:08:33,759 --> 00:08:35,799
Anticipate your opponent's long-term strategy.

150
00:08:36,759 --> 00:08:38,559
Even if a single piece of intel is disproven,

151
00:08:38,759 --> 00:08:40,639
you'll still know how their minds work.

152
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,120
Getting inside their heads—

153
00:08:42,519 --> 00:08:43,879
that's the highest level of intelligence.

154
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:45,720
The best Spear

155
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,399
is a scalpel

156
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,080
that can cut into the skull.

157
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:51,960
I'll remember that.

158
00:08:57,799 --> 00:08:59,440
Your perception is sharp enough,

159
00:09:00,159 --> 00:09:01,279
but you still have a long way to go.

160
00:09:02,399 --> 00:09:03,200
In this line of work,

161
00:09:03,879 --> 00:09:05,159
seeing clearly takes skill,

162
00:09:05,559 --> 00:09:06,960
but enduring is what truly matters.

163
00:09:08,879 --> 00:09:10,200
Perhaps in the near future,

164
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,440
we'll meet again.

165
00:09:12,039 --> 00:09:12,840
Once I redeem myself

166
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:13,879
and serve out my sentence,

167
00:09:14,799 --> 00:09:15,799
our business

168
00:09:16,159 --> 00:09:17,360
will have to keep going.

169
00:09:19,759 --> 00:09:20,559
You know what?

170
00:09:21,039 --> 00:09:22,279
In all the years I've known you,

171
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:25,320
I've never admired you as much as I do today.

172
00:09:27,279 --> 00:09:28,480
When the drinks arrive,

173
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,360
I'm definitely raising a glass to you.

174
00:09:32,919 --> 00:09:34,159
Aren't you afraid of the alcohol ban?

175
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,039
I've already written my self-criticism.

176
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,759
One drink, one reprimand,

177
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,279
in exchange for a secret

178
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,919
and mutual trust.

179
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:44,559
Worth it.

180
00:09:55,559 --> 00:09:56,320
Sir,

181
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,279
your package.

182
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,120
Over the past few years,

183
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:21,120
the "MIB" has had me

184
00:10:21,559 --> 00:10:23,720
acquire land near the dual-use airport

185
00:10:23,919 --> 00:10:24,840
to build a factory.

186
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:28,440
In fact, they're building an underground tunnel

187
00:10:28,759 --> 00:10:30,759
that runs beneath the airport runway.

188
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,679
If war ever breaks out,

189
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:36,480
they'll plant explosives in the tunnel

190
00:10:37,039 --> 00:10:38,720
to blow up the runway

191
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,519
and paralyze the airport.

192
00:10:54,799 --> 00:10:55,840
Even now, she still doesn't know

193
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:57,519
what my real name is.

194
00:11:00,279 --> 00:11:01,240
Once, back then,

195
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,000
she and I were leading a tour group out of town.

196
00:11:03,639 --> 00:11:05,039
Our membership got upgraded,

197
00:11:05,759 --> 00:11:06,960
and on the TV in the hotel room,

198
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,240
my name was displayed.

199
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:11,840
But she assumed Yu Lixia was fake too.

200
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:13,720
She told me

201
00:11:14,039 --> 00:11:15,440
that from the very first day we met,

202
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,919
she knew the name Jinlan was fake.

203
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:21,240
Still, it didn't matter.

204
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:24,159
At first, she simply didn't care,

205
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,799
and later on,

206
00:11:28,759 --> 00:11:29,759
it didn't matter anymore either.

207
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,080
She said, "That's life, isn't it?

208
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:34,679
People just deceive one another.

209
00:11:36,799 --> 00:11:38,240
If you can keep up the lie for a lifetime,

210
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:42,480
that's already a blessing.

211
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,679
What's truly sad is

212
00:11:48,759 --> 00:11:49,840
when you can't even be bothered to lie anymore."

213
00:11:53,039 --> 00:11:54,600
She starts chemotherapy tomorrow.

214
00:11:58,440 --> 00:11:59,600
She probably doesn't want you to see

215
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:00,879
how frail and haggard she'll look.

216
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,159
You know what?

217
00:12:07,879 --> 00:12:09,759
Whenever I hit an insurmountable obstacle,

218
00:12:09,759 --> 00:12:11,039
whenever I'm deeply troubled,

219
00:12:13,759 --> 00:12:14,799
I always dream of her.

220
00:12:15,639 --> 00:12:16,759
I don't know if this counts as

221
00:12:16,759 --> 00:12:18,159
relying on each other for survival.

222
00:12:21,399 --> 00:12:22,440
I just feel that

223
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:26,480
there's pain

224
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,600
I'm willing to share and shoulder with her.

225
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:33,039
Why can't she do the same?

226
00:12:35,799 --> 00:12:37,559
You've already secured a way out for her.

227
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,840
Qiu Tian was coerced by Lin Kanshan.

228
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:43,320
Her cooperation counts as meritorious service,

229
00:12:43,679 --> 00:12:45,159
so she's exempt from criminal punishment.

230
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:47,159
You even found her the best doctors.

231
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,799
You've done everything you possibly could.

232
00:13:39,919 --> 00:13:40,799
Just a moment.

233
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:49,639
Brother Yingjia.

234
00:13:50,039 --> 00:13:51,120
I hope I'm not interrupting.

235
00:13:51,879 --> 00:13:53,720
Isn't that why you came?

236
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,799
Otherwise, coming all this way...

237
00:13:56,159 --> 00:13:57,559
...certainly wasn't just to reminisce.

238
00:13:58,159 --> 00:13:58,799
What's on your mind?

239
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,440
The mainland has been making moves.

240
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:05,440
One after another.

241
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,039
Quite a stir.

242
00:14:08,679 --> 00:14:10,120
The assets I planted over there...

243
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,639
...have all been rooted out.

244
00:14:13,759 --> 00:14:16,360
You probably recall Lin Kanshan.

245
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:17,440
Don't you?

246
00:14:22,519 --> 00:14:24,159
The Chamber of Commerce's deputy secretary-general?

247
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,000
What about him?

248
00:14:26,799 --> 00:14:27,759
He was rooted out too.

249
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,840
That's a real pity.

250
00:14:32,159 --> 00:14:33,639
Isn't it?

251
00:14:34,879 --> 00:14:36,679
The little lamb had barely grown...

252
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,960
...before turning into lamb chops.

253
00:14:39,759 --> 00:14:41,000
It's a shame about his dossier.

254
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:44,000
That's what the Communists needed most.

255
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,799
They're truly impressive.

256
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:49,240
Whatever they want...

257
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,639
...they get.

258
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:52,440
And if they can't...

259
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:55,639
...they have you steal it.

260
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:04,320
Has your blood pressure been acting up?

261
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:07,240
Along with frequent migraines?

262
00:15:10,039 --> 00:15:11,519
High blood pressure...

263
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:12,840
...poor sleep...

264
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:15,039
...can even cause hallucinations.

265
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:17,120
When did they drag you into this?

266
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,000
Your pants are soaked...

267
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,159
...there's mud on your feet...

268
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:24,200
...yet nobody sees it.

269
00:15:26,399 --> 00:15:28,240
Sometimes I wonder...

270
00:15:30,159 --> 00:15:31,600
If it weren't for me...

271
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:34,919
If I weren't here...

272
00:15:36,639 --> 00:15:38,039
Given enough time...

273
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,080
...once you became director...

274
00:15:42,519 --> 00:15:45,720
...the entire "MIB" would turn Communist.

275
00:16:02,919 --> 00:16:04,240
I'm going to see the Director now.

276
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,240
Before I get back,

277
00:16:07,799 --> 00:16:09,039
don't touch my things.

278
00:16:10,759 --> 00:16:11,559
Brother Yingjia,

279
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:14,159
you have a weak stomach.

280
00:16:14,919 --> 00:16:16,320
Don't end up paying dearly.

281
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:19,399
By the way,

282
00:16:20,639 --> 00:16:22,720
I wasn't dragged into this.

283
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:34,919
A traitor.

284
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:37,080
What's so special about him?

285
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,120
Director Wei.

286
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:59,159
Send him and the paperwork to the province tomorrow morning.

287
00:16:59,679 --> 00:17:00,279
Understood.

288
00:17:00,759 --> 00:17:02,240
Open the door. I want to see him.

289
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:03,200
Yes, sir.

290
00:17:08,799 --> 00:17:09,400
This way.

291
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:42,519
Where's the light?

292
00:17:43,079 --> 00:17:44,240
New regulations.

293
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:46,240
No smoking in the entire building.

294
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,240
Just hold it to your nose and smell it.

295
00:17:50,039 --> 00:17:52,240
Is this your new way of humiliating traitors?

296
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:53,920
A cigarette with no light—how cruel.

297
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:55,000
Baoshan must've invented this.

298
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:56,680
If you were really a traitor,

299
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:58,240
I wouldn't give you a single cigarette.

300
00:17:58,519 --> 00:18:00,240
Traitors only get handcuffs.

301
00:18:00,319 --> 00:18:01,359
If it weren't for Old Wu

302
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:04,440
handing over his trump card before retiring,

303
00:18:04,599 --> 00:18:06,200
and if I didn't know you were taking the fall,

304
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,599
you think I'd even talk to you?

305
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:10,680
How does it feel?

306
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,440
Being suspected by your own people,

307
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,119
misunderstood by your own people...

308
00:18:14,279 --> 00:18:16,920
Being a suspect can't feel good, right?

309
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:19,720
I don't see myself as a person.

310
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,640
Being a chess piece is enough.

311
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:23,880
Old Wu said,

312
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:25,200
a strategic piece.

313
00:18:25,359 --> 00:18:26,920
You move me across the Chu River,

314
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,079
and once I reach the Han border,

315
00:18:28,119 --> 00:18:29,680
I'll do something worthwhile

316
00:18:30,119 --> 00:18:31,119
to make up for it.

317
00:18:35,559 --> 00:18:36,440
Old Wu said

318
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:39,160
the brass doesn't care about one city or town,

319
00:18:39,519 --> 00:18:41,359
what they want is strategic value

320
00:18:41,839 --> 00:18:43,160
and far-reaching impact.

321
00:18:43,359 --> 00:18:45,279
The chief back then said the exact same thing.

322
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,799
You all have the exact same lines.

323
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:54,920
Come in.

324
00:18:59,319 --> 00:18:59,960
Director.

325
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:00,680
You're here.

326
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:03,039
Hello, Director.

327
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:07,000
You're much thinner than in your photo.

328
00:19:08,839 --> 00:19:11,039
Ate some leftovers; had an upset stomach these past two days.

329
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:15,240
Tell us your plan.

330
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,960
After Jiang Zaizhen was compromised,

331
00:19:17,039 --> 00:19:19,000
our leg in Taiwan, China was broken.

332
00:19:19,799 --> 00:19:20,599
It has to be reconnected.

333
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:21,960
It'll be difficult,

334
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:22,920
but worth it.

335
00:19:23,279 --> 00:19:23,920
This plan...

336
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:25,079
will take a very long time.

337
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,680
Even starting right now,

338
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,640
it could take over a decade

339
00:19:28,839 --> 00:19:31,480
for the MIB to trust this new leg.

340
00:19:32,359 --> 00:19:35,039
So we need someone to play the traitor.

341
00:19:35,519 --> 00:19:37,960
Someone disgraced and reviled,

342
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:38,960
and perhaps,

343
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,440
a traitor who can never clear his name.

344
00:19:44,279 --> 00:19:46,799
Just like our predecessors during the war,

345
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,519
willing to be unsung heroes.

346
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:50,079
It's not easy.

347
00:19:51,599 --> 00:19:52,519
Sacrificing oneself for others,

348
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,559
braving grave dangers,

349
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:54,640
bearing humiliation in silence,

350
00:19:54,799 --> 00:19:55,680
swallowing bitterness without a word.

351
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:56,960
My plan...

352
00:19:57,960 --> 00:19:59,680
goes beyond what he just mentioned.

353
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:02,160
Replacing Jiang Zaizhen is only the first step.

354
00:20:02,519 --> 00:20:04,640
Your mission is far greater.

355
00:20:05,119 --> 00:20:05,920
Given time,

356
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,559
you must uncover the overseas intelligence network across the Taiwan Strait,

357
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:11,319
and see which forces are interfering behind the scenes.

358
00:20:12,279 --> 00:20:14,039
We want you to be this leg.

359
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,200
What do you think?

360
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,039
He was the one who recruited me.

361
00:20:22,519 --> 00:20:23,680
On my first day on the job,

362
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:25,599
the very first thing he said to me was,

363
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:27,880
"Working in State Security means enduring grievances."

364
00:20:31,119 --> 00:20:31,920
I can handle that.

365
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:34,119
Good.

366
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:39,279
Everyone at the bureau knows

367
00:20:40,079 --> 00:20:42,000
Old Wu got drunk the day he retired.

368
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:43,359
They all thought

369
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:46,079
he was finally unwinding after half a lifetime on edge.

370
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:47,480
Only I knew

371
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:49,480
it was because of you.

372
00:20:50,519 --> 00:20:52,200
He said deploying you as a Spear

373
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,200
was the riskiest move

374
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:55,359
he had ever made in his life.

375
00:20:55,839 --> 00:20:56,759
Like walking on thin ice.

376
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:58,680
He was afraid something would happen to you,

377
00:20:58,680 --> 00:20:59,839
afraid something would go wrong.

378
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,079
Every day, he dreaded the phone ringing.

379
00:21:02,559 --> 00:21:04,039
He longed for news of you,

380
00:21:04,039 --> 00:21:05,640
yet dreaded what he might hear.

381
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:08,799
Old Wu asked me to pass along a message:

382
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,480
Protect yourself.

383
00:21:11,519 --> 00:21:14,000
He would rather have a failed mission

384
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,960
than a colleague who dies a hero.

385
00:21:17,799 --> 00:21:19,279
The Second Division can't lose another Old Lai.

386
00:21:21,839 --> 00:21:23,559
You're all used to calling him Old Lai.

387
00:21:24,359 --> 00:21:25,599
I'm used to calling him Third Brother.

388
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:29,640
In my second year in the division,

389
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,680
I went with Third Brother to tail

390
00:21:32,319 --> 00:21:33,440
Qiao Liang's handler,

391
00:21:33,759 --> 00:21:35,720
that foreign spy who spoke the dialect.

392
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:39,240
To draw attention away

393
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:40,960
and get me out of their sights,

394
00:21:41,559 --> 00:21:42,680
Third Brother put on my coat

395
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,319
and walked eight li in the opposite direction.

396
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:50,160
He ended up wounded.

397
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:52,279
He came back with his arm in a sling,

398
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:54,039
his lips quivering with pain,

399
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:55,920
yet insisted it was nothing.

400
00:21:59,079 --> 00:22:00,680
That night, I stayed by his side at the hospital.

401
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:02,160
He couldn't sleep through the pain,

402
00:22:02,519 --> 00:22:03,519
so he shot the breeze with me.

403
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:05,960
He said in our line of work,

404
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:07,519
most people are Shields.

405
00:22:07,799 --> 00:22:08,279
They must be steady.

406
00:22:09,559 --> 00:22:10,559
But you're different.

407
00:22:11,319 --> 00:22:12,720
You were born to be a Spear.

408
00:22:13,279 --> 00:22:14,440
You have to strike deep.

409
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,400
Even if you break,

410
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:18,400
you must tear open a breach.

411
00:22:21,039 --> 00:22:22,960
I keep thinking back on what he said.

412
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:26,319
If I fail to be the Spear I should be,

413
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:29,559
I'd be unworthy of the hit he took for me.

414
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:32,279
You used to keep badgering me to be a Spear.

415
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:33,519
Now that you are one,

416
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:34,759
are you scared?

417
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:39,039
We're only human.

418
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:41,480
How could I not be scared?

419
00:22:42,759 --> 00:22:44,519
The year my mother died, I was abroad.

420
00:22:45,880 --> 00:22:47,319
One moment I got the text message,

421
00:22:47,839 --> 00:22:50,680
and the next I had to pal around with those foreigners,

422
00:22:51,039 --> 00:22:52,000
cracking jokes for them,

423
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:53,519
laughing right along.

424
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:55,319
By the time I rushed back for the cremation,

425
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:57,400
gazing out the window alone that night,

426
00:22:58,119 --> 00:22:59,400
I found myself wondering too:

427
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:00,480
Was it worth it?

428
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:03,720
What do you think?

429
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:09,680
When the sun comes up the next day,

430
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,559
the work still has to be done.

431
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:13,079
There aren't that many answers.

432
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:15,440
It's not about whether it's worth it.

433
00:23:16,359 --> 00:23:17,599
The path was my own choice.

434
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:20,039
When I chose it, I knew.

435
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:22,559
It's a single-plank bridge with no end in sight.

436
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:24,279
All I can do is brace myself and push forward.

437
00:23:24,519 --> 00:23:25,240
Only by reaching the end

438
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:28,119
can I be worthy of the place Third Brother and the others left,

439
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:29,319
and be worthy of you,

440
00:23:29,519 --> 00:23:31,359
who pulled me out from a pile of files

441
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,160
and put up with me all this time.

442
00:23:34,279 --> 00:23:35,480
The road ahead

443
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:39,440
won't be easy. It'll be rough.

444
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:41,759
You need to be mentally prepared.

445
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,359
You can't prepare for everything.

446
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:45,720
Just brace yourself and keep moving forward.

447
00:23:46,519 --> 00:23:49,119
As for handling the aftermath for me,

448
00:23:49,319 --> 00:23:50,440
you'd better prepare well for that.

449
00:23:54,319 --> 00:23:56,839
The higher-ups want me to explain the situation.

450
00:23:58,559 --> 00:24:00,960
You made things so complicated with Jin Chizhong's gang.

451
00:24:01,359 --> 00:24:02,160
How am I supposed to explain?

452
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:03,920
Why don't you write it yourself?

453
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:05,960
It's simple.

454
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:08,119
To dilute the parameters in Old Jia's intel,

455
00:24:08,119 --> 00:24:09,519
only Cao Liaoping could pull it off.

456
00:24:09,519 --> 00:24:10,920
As for Jin Chizhong and Xiao Lu,

457
00:24:11,079 --> 00:24:12,720
they got out of prison looking for connections everywhere.

458
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:13,920
If I didn't take them in,

459
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:15,720
was I supposed to watch them go work for Taiwan, China?

460
00:24:16,599 --> 00:24:17,519
Cao Liaoping

461
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,160
really did render a service.

462
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:21,720
I didn't lie either.

463
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:24,079
He truly is working for us.

464
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:25,720
Look into it and get the facts straight.

465
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:27,559
He definitely must be granted immunity from punishment.

466
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:29,240
I have to clean up the mess for you again.

467
00:24:30,319 --> 00:24:31,960
It's not like I did nothing.

468
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:33,160
Doing volunteer work,

469
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,839
training newcomers for you for free.

470
00:24:34,839 --> 00:24:36,160
It's fine if you don't pay training fees,

471
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:37,039
but you won't even show some gratitude?

472
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:43,599
Someone is watching you.

473
00:24:44,359 --> 00:24:45,079
One of our own.

474
00:24:45,519 --> 00:24:47,640
Then let's see if he has what it takes to catch me.

475
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:54,160
Europe, the Americas...

476
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:55,319
Eyes all over the world

477
00:24:55,319 --> 00:24:56,599
are watching Huanyu,

478
00:24:56,799 --> 00:24:58,400
all trying to get its technical intel.

479
00:24:58,880 --> 00:24:59,839
There's stuff being sold out there,

480
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:01,039
but most of it is fake.

481
00:25:01,160 --> 00:25:02,559
What Old Jia provided is real.

482
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:04,039
With just a few parameter tweaks,

483
00:25:04,039 --> 00:25:05,279
we can make the fake look genuine.

484
00:25:08,079 --> 00:25:09,160
A real sheep's head,

485
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:11,119
laced with dog meat.

486
00:25:13,480 --> 00:25:15,440
Zheng Guiping will trust you completely.

487
00:25:16,079 --> 00:25:17,279
When I go to Taiwan, China,

488
00:25:17,680 --> 00:25:19,039
and meet him face-to-face,

489
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:21,119
then word gets back here,

490
00:25:21,519 --> 00:25:22,759
and the Second Division, who's been watching me,

491
00:25:23,119 --> 00:25:24,119
moves in to arrest me.

492
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:25,880
The logic will be airtight.

493
00:25:27,079 --> 00:25:27,799
In due time,

494
00:25:27,799 --> 00:25:29,079
after I finish my prison sentence,

495
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,960
I can fully infiltrate Taiwan, China,

496
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:32,799
and become the asset you need.

497
00:25:35,039 --> 00:25:37,240
By then, I'll have a new identity,

498
00:25:37,759 --> 00:25:39,880
back on the overseas intelligence stage.

499
00:25:40,079 --> 00:25:41,960
Where a single cough could sway the situation.

500
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:43,880
That impressive?

501
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:45,440
Aren't you going to congratulate me?

502
00:25:49,519 --> 00:25:50,599
Just as you expected,

503
00:25:51,039 --> 00:25:52,799
under Zheng Guiping's orders,

504
00:25:53,240 --> 00:25:56,000
Chen Leyuan has been asking around about you.

505
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,279
Learning that we arrested you,

506
00:25:57,799 --> 00:25:58,599
she was heartbroken.

507
00:26:00,039 --> 00:26:01,519
The act has to be fully convincing.

508
00:26:01,599 --> 00:26:02,720
The story has to hold up.

509
00:26:02,920 --> 00:26:03,799
Otherwise, how can you expect

510
00:26:03,799 --> 00:26:05,599
anyone in the audience to shed tears?

511
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:10,160
We put in so much work on and off stage.

512
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:12,720
Those seasoned critics across the strait

513
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:14,319
are indeed hard to please.

514
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:17,319
You'll be transferred to the provincial department tomorrow,

515
00:26:18,319 --> 00:26:20,119
and soon to the detention center.

516
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:21,559
Have you ever considered

517
00:26:23,200 --> 00:26:24,279
that all these years in prison...

518
00:26:25,160 --> 00:26:26,079
might be for nothing?

519
00:26:33,519 --> 00:26:34,960
From before the liberation to this day,

520
00:26:35,480 --> 00:26:37,079
so many people buried in Taipei,

521
00:26:38,759 --> 00:26:40,559
many of whom couldn't even keep their names...

522
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:42,279
Did they ever wonder

523
00:26:42,279 --> 00:26:43,359
if all those years

524
00:26:43,559 --> 00:26:44,559
were spent in vain?

525
00:26:48,799 --> 00:26:49,759
None of it was in vain.

526
00:26:50,799 --> 00:26:53,160
Not a single day, not a second,

527
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:53,960
was ever in vain.

528
00:26:57,279 --> 00:26:59,480
Because no matter how dark the road, someone has to walk it.

529
00:27:00,839 --> 00:27:03,279
No matter how vile the disgrace, someone has to bear it.

530
00:27:04,720 --> 00:27:06,039
As long as there's light at the end,

531
00:27:07,559 --> 00:27:08,680
no life was lived in vain.

532
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:28,000
Take care.

533
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:57,039
I'm still tallying the exact number of arrests.

534
00:27:57,039 --> 00:27:59,400
The mainland's Operation Autumn Harvest is hitting hard.

535
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:01,839
Even several sites in the counties were dismantled.

536
00:28:02,400 --> 00:28:04,119
We just can't reach Lin Kanshan.

537
00:28:04,519 --> 00:28:06,359
He's responsible for that plot by the airport.

538
00:28:06,359 --> 00:28:07,920
I'm afraid that might be compromised too.

539
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:10,279
Stop giving me these vague generalities.

540
00:28:10,279 --> 00:28:12,119
Can you give me some actual numbers?

541
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:13,200
What about Ma Qi?

542
00:28:13,480 --> 00:28:15,119
Is there any way to get his sentence reduced?

543
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:18,799
We finally managed to find a Gu Shunzhang,

544
00:28:19,119 --> 00:28:21,119
so why are Qian Zhuangfeis everywhere?

545
00:28:21,519 --> 00:28:22,640
We're already working on a solution.

546
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:23,839
We'll do our best to rescue him.

547
00:28:43,599 --> 00:28:45,079
What's this about?

548
00:28:45,759 --> 00:28:47,559
Did I really have to come in person

549
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:48,799
for you to talk?

550
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:53,880
Recently, State Security organs

551
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:55,200
launched Operation Autumn Harvest,

552
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:56,279
striking with heavy blows,

553
00:28:56,279 --> 00:28:59,079
cracking dozens of espionage cases involving Taiwan, China,

554
00:28:59,079 --> 00:29:01,920
capturing spies and recruited agents from Taiwan, China,

555
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:03,920
and busting multiple intelligence apparatuses of Taiwan, China

556
00:29:03,920 --> 00:29:05,079
that targeted the mainland

557
00:29:05,079 --> 00:29:06,960
to establish espionage networks.

558
00:29:07,240 --> 00:29:08,839
Meanwhile, State Security organs have

559
00:29:08,839 --> 00:29:10,400
carried out anti-secession

560
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:11,680
and counter-espionage struggles regarding Taiwan, China,

561
00:29:11,680 --> 00:29:13,680
crushing any "Taiwan independence" separatist plots,

562
00:29:13,880 --> 00:29:16,160
resolutely countering all moves to rely on external forces for independence

563
00:29:16,160 --> 00:29:17,599
and "use Taiwan to contain China,"

564
00:29:17,799 --> 00:29:19,599
and firmly cracking down on all forms of infiltration,

565
00:29:19,599 --> 00:29:20,799
theft of secrets, and sabotage.

566
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:22,319
This professor in Taipei

567
00:29:22,480 --> 00:29:23,759
claimed on a show

568
00:29:23,759 --> 00:29:26,279
that people on the mainland can't afford tea eggs,

569
00:29:26,279 --> 00:29:27,599
becoming an internet sensation.

570
00:29:27,960 --> 00:29:29,039
Just to boost ratings,

571
00:29:29,039 --> 00:29:29,960
isn't that ridiculous?

572
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:33,319
A brainless show doesn't mean the audience is stupid.

573
00:29:33,319 --> 00:29:36,079
Variety shows rely on comedy, of course,

574
00:29:36,079 --> 00:29:38,359
but this perception also reflects

575
00:29:38,359 --> 00:29:39,640
that cross-strait exchanges

576
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:41,279
need to go much deeper.

577
00:29:41,279 --> 00:29:43,640
I wonder if the staff dinner at the station tonight

578
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:44,960
includes tea eggs.

579
00:29:45,160 --> 00:29:46,359
All the tea eggs you can eat!

580
00:29:46,680 --> 00:29:47,200
Old Wei.

581
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:50,240
Was this TV bought with my prize money?

582
00:29:50,440 --> 00:29:51,039
Yeah.

583
00:29:51,279 --> 00:29:54,279
I heard the mall has a big sale in two days.

584
00:29:54,519 --> 00:29:55,319
Can we return it?

585
00:29:55,559 --> 00:29:57,519
You agreed to offer the money for prizes.

586
00:29:58,000 --> 00:29:58,960
You can't back out now.

587
00:29:58,960 --> 00:29:59,720
I'm not backing out.

588
00:30:00,279 --> 00:30:01,799
Return it first, then buy it back.

589
00:30:01,799 --> 00:30:03,240
That's a difference of several hundred yuan!

590
00:30:04,359 --> 00:30:05,839
What are you doing? Where are you throwing up?

591
00:30:05,839 --> 00:30:06,559
You threw up all over Chief Wu's shoes!

592
00:30:06,559 --> 00:30:07,519
I'm sorry, I'm so sorry!

593
00:30:07,519 --> 00:30:08,440
That's disgusting!

594
00:30:08,799 --> 00:30:10,160
Did we buy it too early?

595
00:30:11,839 --> 00:30:12,720
Didn't we?

596
00:30:16,880 --> 00:30:17,680
Yes, yes, yes.

597
00:30:18,039 --> 00:30:20,240
Right, right, right.

598
00:30:25,480 --> 00:30:26,359
Congratulations.

599
00:30:29,519 --> 00:30:30,319
Congratulations.

600
00:30:32,240 --> 00:30:33,000
Congratulations.

601
00:30:34,079 --> 00:30:34,880
Congratulations.

602
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:37,960
Good work, everyone.

603
00:30:58,319 --> 00:31:00,640
I haven't worn it once since it was issued. Look,

604
00:31:00,839 --> 00:31:03,119
it doesn't fit anymore, can't even button it.

605
00:31:05,799 --> 00:31:06,920
Mine is the same.

606
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:08,599
It fit just right back then,

607
00:31:08,720 --> 00:31:09,559
but now when I put it on,

608
00:31:09,680 --> 00:31:10,519
it's completely baggy.

609
00:31:12,480 --> 00:31:13,920
Am I not looking good anymore?

610
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:16,200
You haven't changed.

611
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:18,559
Just like when I first saw you in the classroom.

612
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:28,559
Why did you lose so much weight? Look,

613
00:31:30,880 --> 00:31:32,079
so much grey hair too.

614
00:31:32,799 --> 00:31:33,599
Let's cover it up.

615
00:31:34,759 --> 00:31:35,559
You're going to be late.

616
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:38,000
I'm never late.

617
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:40,400
If you don't leave now,

618
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:41,640
you really will be.

619
00:31:44,279 --> 00:31:44,960
Time to go.

620
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:35,000
The 12th NPC Standing Committee

621
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:36,480
at its 15th session

622
00:33:36,480 --> 00:33:38,319
recently voted to adopt the new

623
00:33:38,319 --> 00:33:41,720
National Security Law of the People's Republic of China.

624
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:44,480
The law addresses political and homeland security,

625
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:46,799
military and cultural security,

626
00:33:46,799 --> 00:33:48,960
and sci-tech security across 11 fields,

627
00:33:48,960 --> 00:33:51,359
clearly defining national security tasks.

628
00:33:51,359 --> 00:33:53,400
It takes effect on the day of promulgation.

629
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:54,960
Authorized by Xinhua News Agency,

630
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:56,720
the full text of the law has been released.

631
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:59,559
The new law contains seven chapters,

632
00:33:59,559 --> 00:34:02,119
setting out duties in safeguarding national security,

633
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:03,079
Okay.

634
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:04,039
Got it.

635
00:34:04,039 --> 00:34:04,960
systems and safeguards for national security,

636
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,000
When are you leaving?

637
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:08,280
and the rights and duties of citizens and groups,

638
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:09,119
specifying all key provisions.

639
00:34:09,119 --> 00:34:09,639
All right.

640
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:19,360
If the higher-ups hadn't stepped in,

641
00:35:19,920 --> 00:35:22,519
you'd be rotting in prison for the rest of your life.

642
00:35:25,440 --> 00:35:27,159
Go back and enjoy your retirement.

643
00:35:27,480 --> 00:35:29,119
Forget about this little place of ours.

644
00:35:29,599 --> 00:35:31,599
I hope we never see each other again.

645
00:35:36,639 --> 00:35:37,440
We will.

646
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:39,559
Soon.

647
00:35:43,719 --> 00:35:44,800
Trying to scare me?

648
00:37:34,760 --> 00:37:35,559
Welcome back.

649
00:37:40,440 --> 00:37:41,239
Welcome back.

650
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:39,400
Salute!
